we believe now we're well on track having finalized the submission of that data for

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:20.580
an approval inside of q3 next question operator thank you your next question comes from the line

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:26.940
of florence says peders from bernstein please go ahead good afternoon thank you

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:32.460
very much for taking my question a quick question on cost and ticks um and the new indication

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:39.420
in hs could you give us uh some color on how you see the hs opportunity going forward as it seems

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:45.500
that you are gaining new patients as you have a new treatment more potentially the existing one

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:52.380
but there will be also new in trends in the coming years so some color on this hs market

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:58.460
opportunity would be great thank you yeah thanks florent as you know historically uh

00:01:58.460 --> 00:01:58.540
only anti-tnfs adalimumab was the only medicine available for this model and i think that's a very strong

00:01:58.540 --> 00:02:02.140
for the delivery and as you know historically anti-tnf had limumab was the only medicine available

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:08.800
biologic medicine available for these patients. And so I think the market had not grown to its

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:13.960
full potential. I mean, HS is a relatively prevalent dermatological disease. I think

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:19.740
it's second most prevalent after psoriasis, or second or third most prevalent after psoriasis.

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:26.300
So I think it's something that's really a big unmet need. So I would expect there to be a

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:31.940
significant expansion in the market as more entrants come in. And we continue to believe

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:39.180
that Cosentix and HS alone are a billion-dollar medicine. So we're very optimistic on Cosentix,

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:45.400
Outlook, and HS, even with other entrants coming in, simply because there is so much unmet need.

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:50.760
Most patients are not on biologics, or many of these patients have dropped out of the system

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:55.840
and are not receiving care at all. Now that physicians know that there are safe options

00:02:55.840 --> 00:03:01.560
available, we believe more and more patients will be brought in. We see that broad-based globally.

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:08.360
So I mentioned as well, we see strong HS uptake for Cosentix in the U.S., as well as in EU and

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:12.920
international markets. So we think it could be an attractive market in the long run. And we also

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:20.100
have a pipeline we're developing as future agents to follow on for Cosentix in HS. Now in phase

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:25.200
two studies, but over as it matures, we're excited about, can we actually address HS with

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:30.380
even higher efficacy medicines over time? Thank you very much.

